{"id":29038,"slug":"true-stories","title":"True Stories","year":1986,"country":"United States","duration":89,"spine":951,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29038-true-stories","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/7577ed3ce6bab96d5193c4b744e0098a/1xw1IyFisGyE1qcyYVvxGWy8nUZv89_large.jpg","description":"Music icon David Byrne was inspired by tabloid headlines to make his sole foray into feature-film directing, an ode to the extraordinariness of ordinary American life and a distillation of what was in his own idiosyncratic mind. The Talking Heads front man plays a visitor to Virgil, Texas, who introduces us to the citizens of the town during preparations for its Celebration of Specialness. As shot by cinematographer Ed Lachman, Texas becomes a hyperrealistic late-capitalist landscape of endless vistas, shopping malls, and prefab metal buildings. In True Stories, Byrne uses his songs to stitch together pop iconography, voodoo rituals, and a singular variety show—all in the service of uncovering the rich mysteries that lurk under the surface of everyday experience.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"David Byrne","slug":"david-byrne"}],"cast":[{"actor":"John Goodman","role":"Louis Fyne","slug":"john-goodman"},{"actor":"Annie McEnroe","role":"Kay Culver","slug":"annie-mcenroe"},{"actor":"Swoosie Kurtz","role":"Lazy Woman","slug":"swoosie-kurtz"},{"actor":"Spalding Gray","role":"Earl Culver","slug":"spalding-gray"},{"actor":"David Byrne","role":"Narrator","slug":"david-byrne"},{"actor":"Jo Harvey Allen","role":"Lying Woman","slug":"jo-harvey-allen"},{"actor":"Roebuck “Pops” Staples","role":"Mr. Tucker","slug":"roebuck-pops-staples"},{"actor":"Alix Elias","role":"Cute Woman","slug":"alix-elias"},{"actor":"Tito Larriva","role":"Ramon","slug":"tito-larriva"},{"actor":"Matthew Posey","role":"Computer Guy","slug":"matthew-posey"},{"actor":"John Ingle","role":"Preacher","slug":"john-ingle"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"David Byrn